t_run_status\r\n13:from infrastructure.shared.models.text import TextModel\r\n14:from infrastructure.utils.presentation.console import DemoConsole\r\n15:from infrastructure.shared.project.dependencies import install_dependencies\r\n16:from infrastructure.utils.files import save_json\r\n17:from infrastructure.shared.project.git import checkpoint\r\n18:\r\n19:\r\n20:TEST_INSTRUCTIONS = \"\"\"Write one HTTP acceptance suite for task.api before implementing it.\r\n21:Derive expected outcomes from the requirement scenarios, API method/path, I/O, P/Q and DB\r\n22:changes. Use edit_file to create the .test.ts target under backend/tests or update test_path.\r\n23:Use { test } from node:test and assert from node:assert/strict with async test callbacks.\r\n24:Import { createApiTest, fixturePasswordHash } as needed from task.support_module with a\r\n25:relative .js ESM path. Do not import handlers, createApp, server or test aliases.\r\n26:\r\n27:At the start of each test call const { database, baseURL } = createApiTest(t).\r\n28:The compiler owns a real backend process running backend/src/server.ts, its assigned port\r\n29:and its temporary on-disk database. The helper restores prerequisite data before each case\r\n30:and opens that SAME database for Given setup and SQL observations. Test files/cases run\r\n31:sequentially. Do not start a server, choose a port, create a separate database, run tests\r\n32:concurrently, mock HTTP or call business functions directly.\r\n33:\r\n34:Exercise EVERY success/rejection case through real HTTP:\r\n35:const response = await fetch(new URL('/api/example', baseURL), {\r\n36:  method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\r\n37:  body: JSON.stringify({ example: 'value' }), redirect: 'manual'\r\n38:});\r\n39:assert.equal(response.status, expectedStatus);\r\n40:const body = await response.json();\r\n41:Adapt the example to the canonical contract. Substitute encoded concrete route parameter\r\n42:values, construct query strings and JSON bodies, and verify actual status/body/headers.\r\n43:For 204 or other empty responses use text() or skip JSON parsing. Use redirect:'manual'\r\n44:when validating status/Location. Node fetch does not maintain browser cookies: obtain\r\n45:required cookies from real responses using headers.getSetCookie(), strip attributes and\r\n46:send them in a Cookie header for subsequent requests when this API requires it. Supply\r\n47:only contract-required authentication; do not test another requirement's login flow as\r\n48:an incidental dependency. Necessary existing sessions/accounts can be prepared via SQL.\r\n49:\r\n50:Seed only required Given state directly through database with parameterized SQL and valid\r\n51:values; use 0/1 booleans. Read the actual shared helper/SQL definitions rather than guessing\r\n52:fixture arguments or password encodings. Initialization loads db/seeds/ENTITY.sql; reuse\r\n53:existing prerequisites instead of assuming empty tables or duplicating identities. Arrange\r\n54:scenario-specific absence/conflicting states in this isolated database. Do not invoke\r\n55:another requirement's registration/creation API to manufacture Given data.\r\n56:\r\n57:Within max_tests cover meaningful success and critical requirement-defined rejection.\r\n58:Assert relevant persisted results/forbidden writes with SQL where needed; HTTP is the\r\n59:only way to execute the operation. Do not assert unspecified wording, random identifiers,\r\n60:hashes or timestamps. Do not inspect source text, add mocks, skip/focus tests or hardcode\r\n61:success. Browser workflows belong to frontend E2E. Missing routes/behavior should fail real\r\n62:assertions; do not expect 404/501 merely because this API is not implemented yet.\r\n63:\r\n64:The compiler compiles the suite, runs accepted HTTP regressions, then runs this suite\r\n65:against the actual backend. Assertion RED establishes missing behavior. Existing behavior\r\n66:may already be GREEN; no stub replaces it. Backend startup failures are implementation\r\n67:feedback, not proof the test is wrong. During generation repair test syntax/fixtures and\r\n68:existing compilation problems, not the new operation. Generated tests remain correctable\r\n69:against requirement evidence; preserve valid success/rejection coverage and previous tests.\r\n70:\"\"\"\r\n71:\r\n72:IMPLEMENT_INSTRUCTIONS = \"\"\"Implement task.api according to its canonical contract against its generated tests.\r\n73:Read the associated implementation files and extend or create business sources inside the supplied backend scope.\r\n74:Choose meaningful filenames, reuse existing helpers, and extend shared API wiring incrementally. For an API module export:\r\n75:export async function handle(request: ApiRequest, connection: Database.Database): Promise<ApiResponse>.\r\n76:The export is always handle; signature.name identifies the business operation.\r\n77:Tests exercise the operation through HTTP, not through an exported test alias. Import ApiRequest and ApiResponse from backend/src/api/types.ts\r\n78:using a relative .js ESM import. Return status/body/optional headers, not Express objects.\r\n79:\r\n80:Implement request validation, API preconditions, success/rejection responses and DB\r\n81:effects according to the contract and scenarios. Use the supplied connection, parameterized\r\n82:better-sqlite3 SQL, and transactions for related writes. Respect schema-generated integer\r\n83:keys and use node:crypto for UUIDs or hashing when the schema/contract requires them.\r\n84:Use the supplied test utilities and generated tests to understand existing fixture data\r\n85:conventions. Preserve compatibility when reading those records. Production storage must\r\n86:satisfy the contract and keep plaintext passwords out of persistent data.\r\n87:Preserve required comparison rules and shared credential/header conventions.\r\n88:\r\n89:Do not start a server, open another database, change schema or seed production data.\r\n90:Use installed dependencies and Node standard modules. Implement the operation directly;\r\n91:no DB-access primitive layer is generated. The compiler owns the HTTP test runner and fixture.\r\n92:Predefined credentials in seeds/*.sql use seed_password_hash; its scrypt encoding is\r\n93:defined in backend/src/db/seed.ts and must remain readable by credential handlers.\r\n94:Read and edit task.api_wiring.registry to import this handle and register its actual\r\n95:Express route, adapting params/query/body/headers and status/body/headers between HTTP\r\n96:and the handler contract. Inspect app/server wiring when needed. The compiler will not\r\n97:regenerate these files. Preserve all existing routes and middleware; insert/update this\r\n98:API without replacing unrelated registrations or introducing duplicate routes. Extend\r\n99:the existing registerApis implementation; never rebuild its body or route map with only\r\n100:the current API. Earlier requirement implementations remain mandatory. Translate\r\n101:contract path placeholders (including {name}) to syntax accepted by the installed router;\r\n102:pass concrete parameter names and values to handle. Preserve cookies and error handling.\r\n103:Use read_file with optional line ranges, to inspect related wiring; read only the relevant missing\r\n104:lines and use a unique exact edit_file replacement. Do not start the production server in source code.\r\n105:Preserve unrelated behavior when repairing other supplied writable backend sources.\r\n106:Generated tests can be corrected against requirement and API evidence when their\r\n107:expectations or fixtures are wrong or overly strict. Preserve required success and\r\n108:rejection coverage; do not weaken a valid assertion to accept broken behavior.\r\n109:SQL, designs, test utilities and compiler infrastructure remain references.\r\n110:The compiler starts the real server and runs current/accepted HTTP API suites after TypeScript checks. Repair implementation\r\n111:failures without weakening assertions or detecting tests to fake business behavior.\r\n112:\"\"\"\r\n113:\r\n114:\r\n115:def implement_backend_tdd(arc_dir: Path, pause: bool = False, max_turns: int = 10, max_tests: int = 5) -> dict:\r\n---infrastructure/stages/frontend/triggers/implementation.py\r\n1:\"\"\"Complete each leaf requirement through acceptance tests, implementation and regression.\r\n2:\r\n3:Tests derive business expectations from the original requirement. Implementation\r\n4:repairs cannot edit tests. Finish one requirement before advancing, then run final checks.\r\n5:\"\"\"\r\n6:\r\n7:import json\r\n8:\r\n9:from infrastructure.shared.agent.files import editable_application_path\r\n10:from infrastructure.shared.agent.loop import run_file_agent\r\n11:from infrastructure.shared.agent.tools import FileTools\r\n12:from infrastructure.stages.frontend.triggers.acceptance import INSTRUCTIONS as TEST_INSTRUCTIONS, REVIEW_INSTRUCTIONS\r\n13:from infrastructure.shared.agent.recovery import implementation_task, final_checks, complete_report\r\n14:from infrastructure.stages.frontend.triggers.e2e_runtime import CONFIG, FIXTURE, prepare_e2e\r\n15:from infrastructure.stages.frontend.triggers.testing import E2EChecks, test_path\r\n16:from infrastructure.stages.frontend.ui.runtime import APPLICATION_ENTRYPOINTS, prepare_frontend\r\n17:from infrastructure.stages.frontend.ui.testing import FrontendChecks, require_green, test_path as ui_test_path\r\n18:from infrastructure.stages.backend.context import related_schema\r\n19:from infrastructure.stages.backend.runtime import api_test_paths\r\n20:from infrastructure.stages.backend.testing import BackendChecks, require_green as require_backend_green\r\n21:from infrastructure.stages.frontend.triggers.design import api_ids, trigger_obligations\r\n22:from infrastructure.stages.frontend.triggers.scope import TriggerCheckFailure, model_context\r\n23:from infrastructure.shared.project.dependencies import install_dependencies\r\n24:from infrastructure.utils.files import save_json\r\n25:from infrastructure.stages.frontend.ui.design import page_context, page_elements\r\n26:from infrastructure.shared.project.git import checkpoint\r\n27:\r\n28:\r\n29:def scenario_context(ui, design, rid):\r\n30:    \"\"\"Reference this requirement's triggers and directly involved pages only.\"\"\"\r\n31:    triggers = {tid: design[\"triggers\"][tid] for tid in design[\"requirements\"].get(rid, [])}\r\n32:    elements = set(ui[\"requirements\"].get(rid, []))\r\n33:    for trigger in triggers.values():\r\n34:        elements.add(trigger[\"source\"])\r\n35:        for action in trigger[\"action\"]:\r\n36:            if action[\"kind\"] == \"ui\":\r\n37:                elements.add(action[\"ui\"])\r\n38:    pages = {}\r\n39:    for pid in ui[\"pages\"]:\r\n40:        if elements.intersection(page_elements(ui, pid)):\r\n41:            pages[pid] = page_context(ui, pid)\r\n42:    return {\"page_subtrees\": pages, \"triggers\": triggers}\r\n43:\r\n44:\r\n45:def editable_runtime_path(output, path):\r\n46:    \"\"\"Allow evidence-driven database runtime repairs alongside application repairs.\"\"\"\r\n47:    if \"/tests/\" in path:\r\n48:        return False\r\n49:    if editable_application_path(output, path):\r\n50:        return True\r\n51:    return (path.startswith(\"backend/src/db/\") and path.endswith((\".ts\", \".sql\"))\r\n52:        and (output / path).is_file())\r\n53:\r\n54:\r\n55:def test_run_status(result):\r\n56:    \"\"\"Pass every real failure to repair; do not guess its cause from error text.\"\"\"\r\n57:    try:\r\n58:        require_stable_acceptance(result)\r\n59:        return \"GREEN\"\r\n60:    except ValueError:\r\n61:        return \"REPAIR_REQUIRED\"\r\n62:\r\n63:\r\n64:def require_stable_acceptance(result):\r\n65:    require_green(result)\r\n66:    if result.get(\"skipped\") or result.get(\"flaky\"):\r\n67:        raise ValueError(\"Requirement acceptance includes skipped or unstable tests\")\r\n68:\r\n69:\r\n70:IMPLEMENT_INSTRUCTIONS = \"\"\"Implement the current requirement's interactions in the actual application.\r\n71:Step 09's triggers are a reference prototype: preserve their requirement-defined behavior,\r\n72:not a fixed handler/context ABI, event dispatcher, store or routing implementation.\r\n73:Read the actual entrypoints, relevant components and supplied package/configuration first.\r\n74:Use the project's framework and installed dependencies. You own component events, lifecycle\r\n75:hooks, routing, state, input conversion, request construction and response integration.\r\n76:The compiler does not regenerate App, route tables, handlers, stores or API clients.\r\n77:\r\n78:Implement the full path: UI event -> actual input/object identity -> request params/query/\r\n79:body/headers -> real backend API -> success/rejection response -> updated state and visible UI.\r\n80:Use ordinary framework code: closures/callbacks, hooks, services or shared functions as\r\n81:appropriate. You may implement several related reference triggers together in components\r\n82:or helpers. No one-file-per-trigger rule, forced handle export, UiTriggerContext or central\r\n83:registry is required. Keep code reusable and incrementally preserve previous requirements.\r\n84:\r\n85:Preserve explicit original UI naming contracts during implementation and every repair:\r\n86:labels, action names, headings, region names, required placeholders and semantic roles.\r\n87:On pages with breadcrumbs, check that repeated link names do not make primary\r\n88:navigation ambiguous for role-based browser locators. Preserve breadcrumb links,\r\n89:but use a non-navigation wrapper when the original requirement does not demand a\r\n90:second navigation landmark. Repair the real component markup, not the test locator.\r\n91:For a named list/region required by the original contract, verify both its visible\r\n92:heading and semantic landmark. The list container must have role=\"region\" and the\r\n93:exact accessible name, with the real entries inside it. Preserve the data-testid\r\n94:and existing entry click behavior. Check this after a save returns to the parent\r\n95:page, including a newly created Page in the book's Page list.\r\n96:For action controls named Edit or New Page, inspect their semantic role as well as\r\n97:their click behavior. If the original requirement does not explicitly require a\r\n98:link, expose a native button with the exact accessible name and navigate from its\r\n99:click handler. Keep breadcrumb and global navigation links as links; retain the\r\n100:existing data-testid, destination, and operation. Do not add duplicate same-named\r\n101:button/link controls to satisfy different locators. Check this after reload and\r\n102:after a prerequisite creates the object through the UI.\r\n103:For BookStack, the New Page action on the book detail must remain one native\r\n104:button through the final cumulative E2E repair, even when it navigates to a\r\n105:route. Before declaring page publication or reading GREEN, inspect the current\r\n106:book component and run the browser prerequisite with an exact-name button\r\n107:locator. If a later UI change turned it into an anchor, repair the component\r\n108:and rerun the affected existing browser tests. Do not alter the test to click\r\n109:the anchor. Preserve the Page list named region and existing book actions.\r\n110:For BookStack metadata Save Book on an existing book, keep one native form submit\r\n111:that PUTs the same book identity with Name, Description and the retained Tags.\r\n112:On success, close the editor and show the updated level-1 heading and description\r\n113:from the saved values on that same detail route. After reload, load heading and\r\n114:description from persistence; reopening Edit must GET edit metadata and prefill\r\n115:the saved Name, Description and Tags. Do not leave the pre-edit heading visible\r\n116:as the only post-save outcome, invent success without the PUT, drop unchanged\r\n117:tags from the body, or satisfy reopen by reusing only in-memory form state.\r\n118:Cancel must still discard drafts without writing. Preserve Create New Book and\r\n119:delete flows already accepted for earlier requirements.\r\n120:Keep wording, language, spelling and case unchanged; do not add prefixes, translate or\r\n121:concatenate aliases. A required \"Name\" field stays \"Name\". Keep the visible label and\r\n122:computed accessible name consistent; aria-label/aria-labelledby must not replace or extend\r\n123:the required name. Original explicit requirements take precedence over generated design,\r\n124:reference examples and existing incorrect code. Fix a naming violation in the application,\r\n125:not by weakening an otherwise correct test. Unspecified wording remains your choice;\r\n126:dynamic business names and user input must still reflect real data.\r\n127:\r\n128:Before adding an event or effect, read the existing component and follow its current\r\n129:UI -> callback/effect -> service -> HTTP call chain. Extend or reuse the existing owner\r\n130:of that business operation. A new reference trigger ID does not require a new listener.\r\n131:For a form, choose one submission owner; do not send the same mutation from both a\r\n132:button's onClick and the form's onSubmit. Check bubbling handlers, parent callbacks,\r\n133:native listeners and effects as well. Preserve submit-by-Enter and nested-icon clicks.\r\n134:Clean up subscriptions, avoid repeated effect-driven mutations, and use operation-local\r\n135:pending protection for rapid repeated submission when appropriate. Never use a global\r\n136:URL-based deduplication cache to hide duplicate wiring or suppress legitimate operations.\r\n137:\r\n138:For dynamic routes, use the actual router or application routing code to construct and\r\n139:parse concrete parameters. Support direct entry, reload, navigation and back/forward as\r\n140:required. Identify a clicked row from that row's actual data/callback, not a shared global\r\n141:example object or event.target.value from an arbitrary nested icon/span. Carry the selected\r\n142:identity through the URL/request/state consistently; encode URL values correctly.\r\n143:\r\n144:Use framework-native form bindings. An input updates only its actual value field; other\r\n145:variables in element.data may be read dependencies. Choose appropriate types/conversions\r\n146:for numbers, dates, booleans, arrays and other controls. State changes, asynchronous loads,\r\n147:reset/cancel and object switches must update the displayed controls. Do not rely on an\r\n148:automatic compiler input/change handler or require defaultValue/defaultChecked everywhere.\r\n149:\r\n150:Call the canonical backend interfaces with real HTTP, using existing request helpers or\r\n151:new shared application helpers as appropriate. Preserve previous API request cases.\r\n152:Respect response status/body/headers, empty bodies and browser-managed cookies. Do not\r\n153:manually set browser Cookie headers or read HttpOnly credentials. Register event handling\r\n154:only once; preserve action ordering, guards, rejection behavior and failure-without-writes.\r\n155:Keep actual loaded data associated with the requested object. Initialize safe unloaded\r\n156:state and requirement defaults; never seed UI state from reference images/test records.\r\n157:Build edit drafts from real loaded objects and cancel to their snapshots. Handle expected\r\n158:errors visibly and prevent stale requests from overwriting a later selection/result.\r\n159:\r\n160:Only task.target_trigger_ids belong to this implementation task. Other controls on supplied\r\n---CHANGELOG.md\r\n300:or data-testid-only locator does not verify this contract; do not replace the role\r\n301:assertion with a test ID when the generated DOM lacks the landmark.\r\n302:Use concrete routes and object identities; :id and {id} are route patterns, not literal URLs.\r\n303:```\r\n304:\r\n305:### 兼容性、验证与回退\r\n306:\r\n307:本版继承 myagent-004，仅修改上述三处指令并追加此日志。保留已有按钮角色、主导航及面包屑规则，要求保留列表 `data-testid` 和条目点击行为。已做 Python 语法编译、与上一版差异检查及 ZIP 完整性检查。尚未重跑耗费模型额度的 Lite 生成和平台评测，不能宣称通过率提升。回退使用 `myagent/myagent-004.zip`；本版快照为 `myagent/myagent-005.zip`。\r\n308:\r\n309:## myagent-006：防止 New Page 回退为链接（2026-11-16）\r\n310:\r\n311:作业提交对象仍是 Python agent 源码。本版以 myagent-005 为基础，只修改 agent 的生成指令；不直接把 12/12 网页复制进提交包，也不改原始 requirements 或平台测试。12/12 工作区与运行 05 的 `requirements.yaml` 哈希相同。前者在 `website/src/Organize.jsx` 用按钮触发 New Page，后者在 `frontend/src/pages/Book.tsx` 又生成了链接。后者虽有正确的 Page list 命名区域，页面创建和阅读的三项平台测试仍超时。按钮角色是明确的实现差异；平台未提供 helper trace，故仍属有证据的修复方向而非已证实的唯一原因。\r\n312:\r\n313:### 修改 A：验收测试指令\r\n314:\r\n315:文件：`infrastructure/stages/frontend/triggers/acceptance.py`\r\n---input/tests/helpers.ts\r\n1:import { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';\r\n2:import { expect, type Locator, type Page } from '@playwright/test';\r\n3:\r\n4:type Surface = Page | Locator;\r\n5:export const AGREEMENT =\r\n6:  'I have read and agree to abide by Terms of Service and Privacy Policy of 12306.cn.';\r\n7:export const link = (surface: Surface, name: string) => surface.getByRole('link', { name, exact: true });\r\n8:export const button = (surface: Surface, name: string) => surface.getByRole('button', { name, exact: true });\r\n9:export const textbox = (surface: Surface, name: string) => surface.getByRole('textbox', { name, exact: true });\r\n10:// Native password inputs have no implicit textbox role; locate them by the required label.\r\n11:export const passwordField = (surface: Surface, name: string) => surface.getByLabel(name, { exact: true });\r\n12:\r\n13:// Seeded by the scenario environment; tests must not use registration to create this Given data.\r\n14:export const EXISTING_ACCOUNT = {\r\n15:  username: 'taken_traveler', email: 'taken.traveler@example.com', password: 'TakenSmoke!2026',\r\n16:};\r\n17:\r\n18:export async function entry(page: Page) { await page.goto('/'); }\r\n19:export async function openRegistration(page: Page) {\r\n20:  await link(page, 'Register').click();\r\n21:  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/register\\/?$/);\r\n22:  await expect(page.getByRole('combobox', { name: 'Nationality', exact: true })).toBeVisible();\r\n23:}\r\n24:export async function openLogin(page: Page) {\r\n25:  await link(page, 'Login').click();\r\n26:  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/login\\/?$/);\r\n27:  await expect(textbox(page, 'Email/Username/Mobile number')).toBeVisible();\r\n28:}\r\n29:export function newAccount() {\r\n30:  const identity = randomUUID().replace(/-/g, '').slice(0, 20);\r\n31:  return {\r\n32:    username: `smoke-${identity}`, email: `smoke-${identity}@example.com`,\r\n33:    name: `Traveler ${identity}`, passport: `P${identity}`, password: 'Valid-password-123!',\r\n34:  };\r\n35:}\r\n36:export type Account = ReturnType<typeof newAccount>;\r\n37:export async function expectSignedIn(page: Page, account: { username: string }) {\r\n38:  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/$/);\r\n39:  await expect(page.getByText(account.username, { exact: true })).toBeVisible();\r\n40:  await expect(link(page, 'Register')).toHaveCount(0);\r\n41:  await expect(link(page, 'Login')).toHaveCount(0);\r\n42:  await expect(button(page, 'Logout')).toBeVisible();\r\n43:}\r\n44:export async function expectSignedOut(page: Page) {\r\n45:  await expect(link(page, 'Register')).toBeVisible();\r\n46:  await expect(link(page, 'Login')).toBeVisible();\r\n47:  await expect(button(page, 'Logout')).toHaveCount(0);\r\n48:}\r\n49:export async function fillRegistration(page: Page, account: Account) {\r\n50:  const nationality = page.getByRole('combobox', { name: 'Nationality', exact: true });\r\n51:  try {\r\n52:    await nationality.selectOption({ label: 'China' }, { timeout: 1_000 });\r\n53:  } catch {\r\n54:    await nationality.click();\r\n55:    await page.getByRole('option', { name: 'China', exact: true }).click();\r\n56:  }\r\n57:  await textbox(page, 'Name').fill(account.name);\r\n58:  await textbox(page, 'Passport number').fill(account.passport);\r\n59:  await textbox(page, 'Passport expiration date').fill('2099-12-31');\r\n60:  await textbox(page, 'Date of birth').fill('1995-06-15');\r\n61:  await page.getByRole('radiogroup', { name: 'Gender', exact: true })\r\n62:    .getByRole('radio', { name: 'Male', exact: true }).check();\r\n63:  await textbox(page, 'Username').fill(account.username);\r\n64:  await passwordField(page, 'Password').fill(account.password);\r\n65:  await passwordField(page, 'Confirm Password').fill(account.password);\r\n66:  await textbox(page, 'Email address').fill(account.email);\r\n67:  await page.getByRole('checkbox', { name: AGREEMENT, exact: true }).check();\r\n68:}\r\n69:export async function registerAccount(page: Page, account: Account) {\r\n70:  await openRegistration(page);\r\n71:  await fillRegistration(page, account);\r\n72:  await button(page, 'Next step').click();\r\n73:  await expectSignedIn(page, account);\r\n74:}\r\n75:export async function signIn(page: Page, identifier: string, password: string) {\r\n76:  await openLogin(page);\r\n77:  await textbox(page, 'Email/Username/Mobile number').fill(identifier);\r\n78:  await passwordField(page, 'Password').fill(password);\r\n79:  await button(page, 'LOGIN').click();\r\n80:}\r\n81:\r\n82:export async function signOut(page: Page, account: { username: string }) {\r\n83:  await button(page, 'Logout').click();\r\n84:  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/$/);\r\n85:  await expectSignedOut(page);\r\n86:  await expect(page.getByText(account.username, { exact: true })).toHaveCount(0);\r\n87:}\r\n---input/tests/REQ-2.spec.ts\r\n1:// requirement: REQ-2 — Register; the two teaching scenarios.\r\n2:import { expect, test } from '@playwright/test';\r\n3:import { EXISTING_ACCOUNT, button, entry, expectSignedIn, expectSignedOut,\r\n4:  fillRegistration, newAccount, openRegistration, registerAccount } from './helpers';\r\n5:\r\n6:test('SCN-REQ-2-01: Register with a new username and remain signed in after refresh', async ({ page }) => {\r\n7:  await entry(page);\r\n8:  const account = newAccount();\r\n9:  await registerAccount(page, account);\r\n10:  await page.reload();\r\n11:  await expectSignedIn(page, account);\r\n12:});\r\n13:\r\n14:test('SCN-REQ-2-02: Reject an existing username without creating a session', async ({ page }) => {\r\n15:  const account = { ...newAccount(), username: EXISTING_ACCOUNT.username };\r\n16:  await entry(page);\r\n17:  await openRegistration(page);\r\n18:  await fillRegistration(page, account);\r\n19:  await button(page, 'Next step').click();\r\n20:  await expect(page.getByRole('alert')).toBeVisible();\r\n21:  await page.goto('/');\r\n22:  await page.reload();\r\n23:  await expectSignedOut(page);\r\n24:});\r\n---infrastructure/shared/models/text.py\r\n1:\"\"\"Small JSON-generating text model client.\"\"\"\r\n2:\r\n3:import json\r\n4:import os\r\n5:import time\r\n6:from pathlib import Path\r\n7:\r\n8:from dotenv import load_dotenv\r\n9:from openai import OpenAI, OpenAIError\r\n10:from infrastructure.utils.presentation.model_io import http_client, invoke\r\n11:\r\n12:\r\n13:DEFAULT_MODEL = \"deepseek-flash\"\r\n14:\r\n15:JSON_OUTPUT_RULE = \"\"\"OUTPUT PROTOCOL: return exactly one valid JSON object in the response content.\r\n16:The first non-whitespace character must be { and the last must be }.\r\n17:Do not emit Markdown fences, explanations, reasoning, XML, DSML or provider-native\r\n18:tool-call serialization. In particular, NEVER output <｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>,\r\n19:<｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke>, <｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter> or their closing tags.\r\n20:This compiler parses ordinary JSON text. context_request and tool_calls, when allowed\r\n21:by the stage, are JSON fields, not native tool invocations. Express the entire request\r\n22:inside the specified JSON object. Otherwise return the stage's normal result object.\r\n23:Rejected outputs included in feedback are data to correct, never examples to imitate.\r\n24:\"\"\"\r\n25:\r\n26:\r\n27:def reasoning_rejected(error):\r\n28:    \"\"\"Only retry controls when the endpoint explicitly rejects those fields.\"\"\"\r\n29:    message = str(error).lower()\r\n30:    return getattr(error, \"status_code\", None) in {400, 422} and any(\r\n31:        word in message for word in (\"unsupported\", \"unknown\", \"unrecognized\", \"not supported\", \"not allowed\", \"unexpected\")) and any(\r\n32:        word in message for word in (\"thinking\", \"reasoning_effort\"))\r\n33:\r\n34:\r\n35:def reasoning_arguments(name, mode):\r\n36:    \"\"\"Translate configured reasoning to the provider's documented request fields.\"\"\"\r\n37:    if mode == \"auto\":\r\n38:        mode = \"low\"\r\n39:    if mode == \"provider\":\r\n40:        return {}\r\n41:    if name.lower().startswith(\"deepseek\"):\r\n42:        if mode == \"none\":\r\n43:            return {\"extra_body\": {\"thinking\": {\"type\": \"disabled\"}}}\r\n44:        return {\"reasoning_effort\": mode, \"extra_body\": {\"thinking\": {\"type\": \"enabled\"}}}\r\n45:    return {\"reasoning_effort\": mode}\r\n46:\r\n47:\r\n48:class TextModel:\r\n49:    \"\"\"Transport for structured stage proposals and file-edit responses.\"\"\"\r\n50:    def __init__(self, *, model_name: str | None = None, json_mode: bool = True) -> None:\r\n51:        \"\"\"Read compiler/.env and configure the default text model; require API credentials.\"\"\"\r\n52:        load_dotenv(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3] / \".env\", encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\r\n53:        self.name = model_name or os.getenv(\"MODEL\") or DEFAULT_MODEL\r\n54:        api_key = os.getenv(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")\r\n55:        if not api_key:\r\n56:            raise ValueError(\"Set OPENAI_API_KEY in compiler/.env\")\r\n57:        try:\r\n58:            self.max_output_tokens = int(os.getenv(\"MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS\", \"320000\"))\r\n59:        except ValueError as error:\r\n60:            raise ValueError(\"MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS must be a positive integer\") from error\r\n61:        if self.max_output_tokens < 1:\r\n62:            raise ValueError(\"MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS must be a positive integer\")\r\n63:        self.reasoning = os.getenv(\"MODEL_REASONING\", \"low\").lower()\r\n64:        if self.reasoning not in {\"auto\", \"provider\", \"none\", \"low\", \"high\", \"max\"}:\r\n65:            raise ValueError(\"MODEL_REASONING must be auto, provider, none, low, high or max\")\r\n66:        self._reasoning_supported = True\r\n67:        self.json_mode = json_mode\r\n68:        self._token_parameter = \"max_completion_tokens\"\r\n69:        self.client = OpenAI(\r\n70:            api_key=api_key,\r\n71:            base_url=os.getenv(\"OPENAI_BASE_URL\") or \"https://api.openai.com/v1\",\r\n72:            timeout=600, max_retries=2,\r\n73:            http_client=http_client(),\r\n74:        )\r\n75:\r\n---infrastructure/shared/models/vision.py\r\n1:\"\"\"Minimal visual model client using the existing model environment variables.\"\"\"\r\n2:\r\n3:import base64\r\n4:import json\r\n5:from io import BytesIO\r\n6:import mimetypes\r\n7:import os\r\n8:from pathlib import Path\r\n9:\r\n10:from dotenv import load_dotenv\r\n11:from openai import OpenAI, OpenAIError\r\n12:from PIL import Image, ImageOps\r\n13:from infrastructure.utils.presentation.model_io import http_client, invoke\r\n14:from infrastructure.utils.presentation.console import DemoConsole\r\n15:from infrastructure.shared.agent.proposals import propose_json\r\n16:from infrastructure.shared.models.text import DEFAULT_MODEL, JSON_OUTPUT_RULE, reasoning_arguments, reasoning_rejected\r\n17:\r\n18:\r\n19:VISION_INSTRUCTIONS = \"\"\"Describe the supplied UI reference using visible evidence only.\r\n20:Return {\"layout\":\"...\", \"elements\":[\"...\"], \"style\":\"...\"}.\r\n21:layout describes regions, alignment and relative positions; elements lists visible\r\n22:controls, labels, options and states; style describes colors, typography and spacing.\r\n23:Write descriptions in English while quoting